{
  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine, a nasal decongestant, is shown to bind to Cyp2c8 through multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role in its metabolic activation. The evidence indicates that Brompheniramine interacts with Cyp2c19 and Cyp2e1, both of which are involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics. Cyp2c19 is part of the Diclofenac Metabolic Pathway, while Cyp2e1 is associated with the Epoxygenase and Monooxygenase activities, which are relevant to the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These pathways collectively suggest that Brompheniramine may influence Cyp2c8 through the activation of cytochrome P450 enzymes, potentially affecting the metabolism of substrates that are metabolized by Cyp2c8. The consistent binding to Cyp2c19 and Cyp2e1, along with their participation in metabolic pathways involving Cyp2c8, supports a mechanistic link between Brompheniramine and Cyp2c8. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected role of Cyp2c8 in drug metabolism, reinforcing the possibility of a direct or indirect interaction between Brompheniramine and Cyp2c8.",
